    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO" softwareId="24020486" softwareVersionNum="2024v5.2">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE FOUNDATION'S ACCOUNTANT VERIFIES ACCURACY OF FINANCIAL DATA, FORWARDS THE TAX RETURN TO THE BOARD CHAIRMAN, TREASURER, AND AUDIT CHAIR FOR REVIEW. ONCE REVIEWED THE TAX RETURN IS PRESENTED TO THE BOARD, WHERE IT IS APPROVED AND SIGNED BEFORE FILING THE TAX RETURN.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TO ENSURE THAT THE FOUNDATION OPERATES IN A MANNER CONSISTENT WITH CHARITABLE PURPOSES AND DOES NOT ENGAGE IN ACTIVITIES THAT COULD JEOPARDIZE ITS TAX-EXEMPT STATUS, PERIOD REVIEWS ARE CONDUCTED. REVIEWS INCLUDE WHETHER COMPENSATION ARRANGEMENTS AND BENEFITS ARE REASONABLE AND WHETHER PARTNERSHIPS, JOINT VENTURES, ARRANGEMENTS WITH MANAGEMENT ORGANIZATIONS CONFORM TO THE FOUNDATION'S WRITTEN POLICIES, ARE PROPERLY RECORDED, REFLECT REASONABLE INVESTMENT OR PAYMENTS FOR GOODS AND SERVICES, FURTHER CHARITABLE PRUPOSES AND DO NOT RESULT IN INCREMENT, IMPERMISSIBLE PRIVATE BENEFIT OR IN AN EXCESS BENEFIT TRANSACTION. BOARD OF DIRECTORS ARE ALSO REQUIRED TO COMPLETE FORM 700 STATEMENT OF ECONOMIC INTERESTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS USES INFORMATION ABOUT AN INDIVIDUALS EXPERIENCE ALONG WITH COMPARABLE SALARIES IN THE MARKET TO DETERMINE COMPENSATION FOR THEIR EMPLOYEES. THE FOUNDATION HAS AN AD-HOC COMMITTEE, THEY REVIEW CURRENT PAY SCALES AND A DECISION ABOUT EXPENSE RATIOS IS USED. THE FOUNDATION'S MANAGEMENT/OFFICERS CONSISTS OF THEIR BOARD OF DIRECTORS WHICH ARE ALL NON-COMPENSATED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS USES INFORMATION ABOUT AN INDIVIDUALS EXPERIENCE ALONG WITH COMPARABLE SALARIES IN THE MARKET TO DETERMINE COMPENSATION FOR THEIR EMPLOYEES. THE FOUNDATION HAS AN AD-HOC COMMITTEE, THEY REVIEW CURRENT PAY SCALES AND A DECISION ABOUT EXPENSE RATIOS IS USED. THE FOUNDATION'S MANAGEMENT/OFFICERS CONSISTS OF THEIR BOARD OF DIRECTORS WHICH ARE ALL NON-COMPENSATED.</ExplanationTxt>
